  "report": "The `test-planner` skill (v0.1.0) is built, linted, and recorded. Everything is in the output folder; nothing in the repository was edited.\n\n**Files produced** (all under `runs/skill-smith/60afa5a8b01e7a8c/output/`)\n- `src/skills/test-planner/`: `SKILL.md` (65 lines), `RULES.json` (R-test-planner-1 to 12), `CHANGELOG.md`, `preview.json`, `preview/cover.svg`, the ten core layers, `references/README.md`, `examples/README.md`, `evals/cases.json` (4 cases) and `evals/live/` (4 recordings).\n- `dist/test-planner-0.1.0.zip`, packed with the factory's own packer (sha256 `431d2456…c257`).\n- `registry-entry.proposed.json` (status `draft`).\n- `EVIDENCE.md`: the full record, including the review answers.\n\n**Checks**\n- Factory linter (`lint-skills`): no problems.\n- Live evals: 4 passed, 0 failed. Each recording comes from a fresh agent given only the skill folder and the case prompt. The checkout and cart-limit replies cite a source phrase for every item and list the unnamed adjacent areas as questions. The negative case refused to write test code, and the no-change-text case asked for the change.\n- Repository `npm test`, `npm run guard`, `run-skill.mjs`, and `routing-evals.mjs` were not run. They write into the repo or only cover registered `ready` skills.\n- The cover was not checked visually in light and dark themes.\n\n**Open items**\n- The skill is in the output folder, not `src/skills/`. Moving it, adding the registry entry, and writing `runs/` and `dist/` into the repo are owner decisions.\n- The registry proposal's `roles` (BA_ANALYST, QA_AUDITOR) are my guess; confirm or change them.\n- The `EVIDENCE.md` review is my own self-check, not an independent review. The owner should confirm it before status `ready`.\n- `skill-smith`'s own eval case for this prompt expects the skill inside the repository, so it will only pass after the folder is moved there."
